{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"desirous-consistent-whimbrel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml:68-184,397` invokes third-party major tags in a workflow with contents/actions-write and OIDC capability. Existing full-SHA enforcement covered release flow but not this privileged reconciliation path.\n\n## Approach\n\nReplace every mutable third-party action reference in the reconciliation workflow with its reviewed full commit SHA and preserve readable version comments. Extend the existing actionlint/zizmor/pin contract to cover this workflow.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`\n- `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py`\n- security-lint configuration only if needed to include the workflow\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the existing pin, actionlint, and zizmor checks with a mutable-tag negative fixture/control.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every third-party action in `reconcile-bridge.yml` is referenced by a full SHA with a readable version comment.\n- [ ] Existing actionlint and zizmor coverage include the credentialed/OIDC reconciliation workflow.\n- [ ] The pin test fails for a mutable tag in that workflow.\n- [ ] Normal CI workflow behavior is otherwise unchanged and focused security checks pass.","id":"1c70-319a-2ded-43f9","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":2,"tags":["janitor","security","ci","rp33"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"SHA-pin third-party actions in the privileged reconciliation workflow"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788314093335214001,"uuid":"ff6709e6-f43c-45b3-b14c-979c46780345"}